# The files that "go generate ./..." writes (12 12.3) are compared byte
# for byte, in the working tree and in the index. "-text" keeps git from
# converting their line endings, so a "text eol=crlf" rule of a user's
# configuration cannot make a checkout differ from what generate gives.
# This list does not stop a later line, a .gitattributes in a directory
# or a clone's .git/info/attributes from setting the attribute again;
# "go run ./tools/ci generated" holds it instead: each line names an
# output of generate and each output has a line, and "git check-attr
# --cached" must report "unset" for every output, nested files included.
.github/CODEOWNERS -text
docs/reference/ask-first.md -text
docs/adr/README.md -text
